  490|  8.37M|                // iteration over our collected states to finalize our DFA
  491|  8.37M|                // state. In theory, we could avoid this second iteration if
  492|  8.37M|                // we maintained two sets during epsilon closure: the set of
  493|  8.37M|                // visited states (to avoid cycles) and the set of states that
  494|  8.37M|                // will actually be used to construct the next DFA state.
  495|  8.37M|                //
