  535|  8.37M|                // case, you get: [2, 6, 3]. Notice that '6' is the match state
  536|  8.37M|                // and appears AFTER '3' in the former case. This leads to a
  537|  8.37M|                // preferential but incorrect match of '%' before returning
  538|  8.37M|                // a match. In the latter case, the match is preferred over
  539|  8.37M|                // continuing to accept the '%'.
  540|  8.37M|                //
